TEXT -72 48 Left 3 ;RESONANCE EMULATOR  --  cavity preamp board, post-pan stage
TEXT -72 80 Left 2 ;Gyrator-based series-resonant branch shunting the gain leg.\nRun gyrator_z.cir first: if the port is not inductive, nothing here means anything.\nPlot V(OUT)/V(IN) in dB.   Design and theory: resonance-emulator.md
TEXT 296 688 Left 2 ;large: keeps the\npassband at unity
TEXT -56 440 Left 2 ;BOOST\ntrimmer
TEXT -184 712 Left 2 ;TONE\nplayer\ncontrol
TEXT -152 904 Left 2 ;PA looks like an inductance\nL = R1*R2*Cg to VREF
TEXT 576 1072 Left 2 ;FREQUENCY trimmer
TEXT 920 792 Left 2 ;THE GYRATOR\nThe amplifier integrates the port voltage and inverts it; Rgy2 feeds\nthat back, so the current it injects opposes the applied voltage more\nand more strongly as frequency falls -- which is what an inductor does.
TEXT 856 224 Left 2 ;supply and mid-rail reference
TEXT -80 1104 Left 2 !.inc gyrator.lib\n.param Vrail=3.7  Rf=10k  Rg=1meg\n.param Rb=2.2k  Cs=6.8n  Cg=100p  Ct=22n  Rt=10meg\n; frequency trimmer as a potentiometer: R1+R2 held at 260k\n.param Rend1=150k  Rpot=100k  Rend2=10k\n.param x=0.5\n.param R1={Rend1+Rpot*x}  R2={Rend2+Rpot*(1-x)}\n.ac dec 200 20 40k\n; freq trimmer\n.step param x 0 1 0.125\n; boost trimmer\n;.step param Rb list 2.2k 5k 9k 14k 22.2k
TEXT 960 1104 Left 2 ;Uncomment ONE at a time -- LTspice runs the cross product otherwise:
TEXT 952 1136 Left 2 ;.step param R2 list 47k 82k 147k 200k 247k     (frequency trimmer)
TEXT 952 1168 Left 2 ;;.step param Rb list 2.2k 5k 9k 14k 22.2k        (boost trimmer)
TEXT 952 1200 Left 2 ;;.step param Rt list 100 2k 6k 15k 40k 100k      (tone control)
